  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Ecs Federal obligated $432M in FY2026 to date across 120 awards, with an average award size of $3.6M. Obligations fell 25.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations peaked at $581M in FY25 and declined to $432M in FY26. The Department of Defense and the General Services Administration are the largest buyers, obligating $144M and $135M respectively. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market, accounting for $197M of obligations. Other concentrated markets include All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services with $69.5M, and Engineering Services with $58.8M. The dataset shows the Department of Justice obligated $69.1M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $27M in FY2026 to date. Several smaller agencies bought services, including the Consumer Product Safety Commission with $870K and the Department of Agriculture with $695K. NASA shows no obligations in FY2026 to date, recorded as $0.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Ecs Federal obligated $494M in FY21, $394M in FY22, $473M in FY23, $480M in FY24, $581M in FY25, and $432M in FY26. Obligations fell 25.7% year over year from FY25 to FY26. The FY25 level of $581M is the highest reported in the series. FY22 shows the lowest level in the series at $394M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies account for the largest FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $144M in obligations, followed by the General Services Administration with $135M. The Department of Justice obligated $69.1M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $27M. Several other agencies contributed smaller totals, including HHS with $26.2M and the Department of Commerce with $24.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
